  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 0.4.0, package.json says 0.1.0.",
        "  The App Store and the server read info.xml; everything on the node side reads package.json. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying two version numbers, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "docs/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Controller/ZgwOpenApiController.php:165 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "public/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Controller/DashboardController.php:68 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk), so the tarball lacks them and the app fails in the code that reads them, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += docs public ships them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "3 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/password-confirmation, commander, terser-webpack-plugin.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 4,215 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
